r we get away from  the river so what we do is we have a  starting point which would be right here  where we put our quadrat down what we  then want to do is we want to reposition  our quadrat at equal intervals slowly  going away from our particular point of  interest so let's say for example if  that one's at zero meters this one's at  two meters then four meters then six  meters then eight meters so every single  time what we're going to do is when we  put down the quadrat we're looking at  two things first of all we need to count  the number of organisms that are within  that quadrat and secondly we need to use  some kind of probe or sensor in order to  figure out the kind of how much of that  abiotic factor we have so in this  particular instance what we're going to  be using is a water sensor to see how  much water is in the soil here here here  here and here and Counting how many  plants or how many daisies we have in  each of these different quadrants as  well now different abiotic factors we  could investigate we could be looking at  the effect of light intensity so we  might need a light meter at each of  these settings to read how bright it is  we could also use a temperature probe to  see the temperatures at each of these  places so after we've done the belt  transect at once we just need to repeat  it a couple of times in order to collect  more data so again exactly the same  technique but this time a little bit  further along so here's my five quadrats  that I put down again and then I need to  repeat it at least three times and each  time are putting down the quadrat I'm  counting the number of organisms or this  case daisies that I'd have at each of  these intervals again evenly spread even  the distance so once I've done that what  I can do is I find my average number if  I take the mean number of plants for  these three so I add up the number of  organisms found in each of these three  and in this case because there's three  of them I divide by three I'd do the  same for the abiotic factors so I find  the reading on my water sensor and I  find the average also the mean value for  these three once I've collected all the  data I can hopefully draw a conclusion  to see how does the level of water  affect the distribution of daisies along  a belt transect and that's basically it  thank you
 

